  "query_preview": "(This evening through Friday)...\nIssued at 215 PM EDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nRest of This Afternoon through Saturday...\n\nForcing continues to shift south this afternoon, keeping the bulk of \nthe rain south of central Indiana. There could be some \nsprinkles/light drizzle in the south as some light returns have been \nseen on radar. Will keep some low PoPs south, diminishing from the \nnorth as the afternoon progresses.\n\nClouds will take longer to diminish though. Lower clouds will \ndiminish first, then mid and high clouds will eventually exit as \nwell. Skies likely won't be mostly clear all areas until during the \novernight.\n\nHigh pressure will rule Saturday into Saturday night, providing \nquiet conditions. Some high clouds will move in from the south later \nSaturday into Saturday evening. Otherwise, skies will be mostly \nclear.\n\nLows tonight and Saturday night will be in the 40s to around 50. \nHighs Saturday will be in the mid 60s to lower 70s.\n\nSunday onward...\n\nNorthwest flow aloft will continue across central Indiana next week. \nAt the surface, high pressure will be in control for most of the \nperiod.\n\nA cold front will move through on Sunday, but the front won't have \nany moisture to work with as the Gulf is cut off. Another cold front \nwill move in around Thursday night, but it too will have limited or \nno moisture to work with. Thus, will go with a dry forecast \nthroughout the week.\n\nTemperatures will rebound to above normal on Sunday ahead of the \nfront, then return to below normal for Monday and Tuesday. Low \ntemperatures may fall into the upper 30s across the northeastern \nforecast area Monday night. With light winds and mostly clear skies, \nwill have to watch for the potential for patchy frost in favored \ncold areas.\n\nAs high pressure moves east of the area mid-week, southerly winds \nwill bring back temperatures to above normal. There is some \nuncertainty on how much cooler air will be behind the late week cold \nfront. Present indications that not much cooler air will move in \nbefore upper heights rise again and bring in warmer air beyond the 7 \nday period.",
